The function `verify_header` contains the vulnerable logic on lines 648-650: 
c
	/* read the namespace if present */
	if (!unpack_str(e, ns, "namespace"))
		*ns = NULL;

This unconditionally overwrites the `ns` pointer. If a namespace was successfully unpacked in a previous iteration of a multi-profile stream, a subsequent iteration that does not contain a namespace will overwrite `*ns` with `NULL`, leaking the previously allocated namespace string. Additionally, `unpack_str` on line 247 unconditionally resets `*string = NULL` at the beginning of its execution, which also contributes to the overwrite.
